{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_64e50074d85103060014dfd2e404f3e16bc8ddc9960953cf5e4abbb269b2dbcc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"mvanhorn/agentcookie@57b53dfd9162 snapshot 14f23d6052e3cd81","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0dcea1f5d673ac6fc2889fe4d8bc17605610b812a210adb25c489afe48dadb80","slc_32ee6e2adef4b4297fa041d46cad2d8ff7177640f943624e7fd35194902d77c2","slc_42ec2c7d0ea9cd3953c6866db42248a2b2be17801f09fdf1a88a7acfd38b64fb"],"source_ids":["src_55dfcec9a5085a97866e4ed74cec5710","src_aa0a3da2a74b5c549a74b52329b95a00","src_e274ec2eb4135ca694d54c11b952f1f9"],"text":"The product requires Tailscale and Chrome on both machines, and the Linux sink must bind a Tailscale 100.x address, refusing to start without the tailnet.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6e5b51b9f28b3198359239f7bf0607ffac6d2ad00667c36b734e911c0270ef58","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"mvanhorn/agentcookie@57b53dfd9162 snapshot 14f23d6052e3cd81","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2e4c9655f36969f3e39cb866d662426f51fbbba71108990b47a3c9aedf543236","slc_9d3128955e3889ca1ac8c35bc5cd62b1706be3cf5fd20071f05041eaf67870ed","slc_b07188b4889f2171d39897849fe584a53be4ace411cbdcea2da796054403fb69","slc_ef699c9513d2db0fdb4e9450782d7be672a4e05b624504023017061a32c441d3"],"source_ids":["src_e274ec2eb4135ca694d54c11b952f1f9"],"text":"Chrome's DBSC binds Google/Workspace sessions to device keys, so copied cookies for such sites stop working within minutes; the documented workaround is signing the sink's Chrome into the same Google account locally.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7256e87791e180d626c0c934abb3abb1ec3b4dc5357f284109e1efaad611ee31","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"mvanhorn/agentcookie@57b53dfd9162 snapshot 14f23d6052e3cd81","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2e4c9655f36969f3e39cb866d662426f51fbbba71108990b47a3c9aedf543236"],"source_ids":["src_e274ec2eb4135ca694d54c11b952f1f9"],"text":"Documented limits include a plaintext-at-rest sidecar at ~/.agentcookie/cookies-plain.db, a loopback-only CDP port that same-user processes can read, no live key rotation (wizard re-run required), and unread Linux extra-profile Chrome SQLite.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_856e0652a55416bf71836e48d841e20d891b59ab0ea81d7d9fa4afa804896462","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"mvanhorn/agentcookie@57b53dfd9162 snapshot 14f23d6052e3cd81","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2258385578b48c7198800f1b832380203448861f90fb03795f1b333884106b15","slc_36e44491d7f49bedc881916d8a13c7f452462dc9499cacd65a6b1e7044ad42d1","slc_b754624343542ffdc086eff87a61d69805a290bf76cd7c805cc61d4fd398d2c4"],"source_ids":["src_aa0a3da2a74b5c549a74b52329b95a00"],"text":"The sync protocol carries a versioned SyncEnvelope with a monotonic Sequence; the sink rejects wrong keys with 401, version mismatches with 400, and replays via an in-memory SequenceTracker with 409.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_883b948f84a528007a60465948774ffebb85547487ba73c9af168c262550a91f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"mvanhorn/agentcookie@57b53dfd9162 snapshot 14f23d6052e3cd81","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_32ee6e2adef4b4297fa041d46cad2d8ff7177640f943624e7fd35194902d77c2","slc_6a18889519f16d6d336617e3d4c8d6bebbb7a27f73489abbb5454d91c367a133","slc_6f933d0d58724d97d18f4c7e559f6e4bdba0907567a5a5b8c6e10f1c9622d6bc","slc_8bad1f207eb655ae71f940ec4b8a882c8ba0e49f35acc94117e6a3b92431a7a5"],"source_ids":["src_aa0a3da2a74b5c549a74b52329b95a00","src_e274ec2eb4135ca694d54c11b952f1f9"],"text":"On Linux the sink injects cookies directly into Chrome's in-memory store via the Chrome DevTools Protocol (Storage.setCookies) instead of rewriting Chrome's SQLite, and Chrome must be started with a remote-debugging port such as 9223.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8d6fc2d31418ac32fc0e08e547f64d2584594935ea06f01db111b7b5f0cddc09","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"mvanhorn/agentcookie@57b53dfd9162 snapshot 14f23d6052e3cd81","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_cb133efc3d83be2ba4232b0a19413f275233807a399e98fbc5f8eade3e264d51"],"source_ids":["src_e274ec2eb4135ca694d54c11b952f1f9"],"text":"Repository development practice: the README's working-today list cites 520+ unit tests across 26 packages, a repository test-suite figure rather than any agent-performance evaluation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_91834bd6d42db94bc7be4e4c04a3ffd9aa54c988570999df7e25a41d21e6b36b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"mvanhorn/agentcookie@57b53dfd9162 snapshot 14f23d6052e3cd81","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_36e44491d7f49bedc881916d8a13c7f452462dc9499cacd65a6b1e7044ad42d1","slc_60b5227ed191ade19bd47fcc3963926b2e561b13062f84528f663bf5930fbb71","slc_aaafdff3b3b7c61fc1ad476c7f1226e136b2afcb04d728023c584ef16b99dcbd","slc_d5edea7563807b7a409e7ee6bc4335c94fde75d6485d97b078245b7b2aeb575e"],"source_ids":["src_aa0a3da2a74b5c549a74b52329b95a00","src_e274ec2eb4135ca694d54c11b952f1f9"],"text":"Cookies are sealed with AES-GCM using per-peer keys derived from an X25519 + HKDF pairing handshake in which the pairing code is mixed into the HKDF salt; key files are stored mode 0600.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a4ebb241bef483db16875c3200ded1bc1161a8e5fda6c40278524e8292397151","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"mvanhorn/agentcookie@57b53dfd9162 snapshot 14f23d6052e3cd81","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_275ca68091456a66b7fd1e4b972cf16e6226ae119543aa3b1f34e1dd030eef3b","slc_4cd8a4ac1c4748f54d6d57fb94a3be325420c7bae985eba559fd7c02126847c9"],"source_ids":["src_e274ec2eb4135ca694d54c11b952f1f9"],"text":"One source can fan out to multiple sinks, reading and filtering cookies once then sealing and POSTing to each sink with that sink's own paired key; an unreachable sink fails in isolation, and every sink receives the full cookie and secret set.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bdbef00468a7bee0142a460ce108d9509a632462ac71580b6fcee6f34f3ba592","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"mvanhorn/agentcookie@57b53dfd9162 snapshot 14f23d6052e3cd81","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1968cc094d1efd9d2d0452edd16d833224a30f066f764c5b44ece220e54bab70","slc_60a609b63115ff4fde34fbfa01e059eece091afddeec8806c7049f74e78d5ffa","slc_76050c1b47535b02b3ea22addc55047afa4f39c5cb88c8f57df1acdd2c2d294a","slc_fef0e04909089f39e2138d2f7bf0f1ec4825035c86f9a65d5b6cc861391614ca"],"source_ids":["src_55dfcec9a5085a97866e4ed74cec5710","src_aa0a3da2a74b5c549a74b52329b95a00","src_e274ec2eb4135ca694d54c11b952f1f9"],"text":"On Linux, a missing blocklist.yaml or omitted policy field means the sink ships nothing (allowlist-empty) as a security default; sync-all requires an explicit blocklist policy with an empty domains list, described as an operator choice rather than the code default.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
